WEBVTT

02:25.125 --> 02:31.125
LOOK BACK

02:54.958 --> 03:00.916
STORY IDEAS
AYUMU FUJINO

03:08.458 --> 03:10.375
FIRST KISS

03:10.958 --> 03:15.166
RATTLE
SQUEAK

03:15.291 --> 03:16.291
HOWL

03:16.375 --> 03:19.166
I'm surprised you remember
something from so long ago.

03:19.250 --> 03:21.000
I keep a diary, you see.

03:21.416 --> 03:24.416
Look. Isn't it a cute diary?

03:24.500 --> 03:25.333
Yeah.

03:27.333 --> 03:28.166
HOWL

03:29.833 --> 03:30.666
SCREECH

03:32.250 --> 03:33.541
SPIN
CRASH

03:33.791 --> 03:34.666
ROLL
SKID

03:37.625 --> 03:38.458
BANG!

03:38.541 --> 03:39.375
SMOKE

03:39.458 --> 03:42.291
RIGHT BEFORE THEY DIE IN THE ACCIDENT

03:42.666 --> 03:46.458
Kiss me again when we're reincarnated.

03:48.750 --> 03:49.583
COUGHS

03:51.125 --> 03:52.833
I promise I will.

04:03.833 --> 04:04.666
YEAR 0

04:04.750 --> 04:05.750
YEAR 3

04:05.833 --> 04:06.875
YEAR 10

04:06.958 --> 04:08.250
YEAR 17

04:08.875 --> 04:09.708
20 YEARS LATER

04:09.791 --> 04:10.958
I've been reincarnated!

04:11.041 --> 04:13.250
Honey, where are you?

04:15.875 --> 04:16.791
RUMBLE RUMBLE

04:19.833 --> 04:22.083
NIKAHO CITY

04:22.166 --> 04:23.000
HIMAWARI SATELLITE

04:23.083 --> 04:24.791
EARTH

04:25.791 --> 04:27.208
EARTH

04:27.291 --> 04:28.708
RUMBLE

04:36.750 --> 04:37.708
4TH GRADE NEWSPAPER

04:37.791 --> 04:41.625
LETTER FROM AN ALIEN BY FUJINO
FIRST KISS BY FUJINO

04:42.208 --> 04:43.083
All right.

04:43.166 --> 04:45.708
I'm handing out this week's newspaper.

04:46.291 --> 04:48.541
Don't forget to show it to your parents.

04:57.625 --> 04:59.291
The drawings are so good.

04:59.750 --> 05:03.083
Fujino, this week's four-panel
manga strips were really funny!

05:05.083 --> 05:06.541
Oh, these.

05:06.625 --> 05:09.625
I was kind of busy this week,
so I drew it in five minutes.

05:10.291 --> 05:13.916
But I guess they turned out
pretty good despite that.

05:14.500 --> 05:18.000
You could be a manga artist
when you grow up.

05:19.916 --> 05:23.375
A manga artist? Maybe.

05:23.916 --> 05:27.041
But sitting at a desk
drawing all day sounds boring.

05:27.125 --> 05:30.750
You're good at sports too,
so why not be an athlete?

05:30.833 --> 05:33.125
Yeah, that sounds better.

05:33.208 --> 05:35.458
Either way, give me your autograph.

05:35.541 --> 05:37.250
Okay, fine.

05:37.333 --> 05:38.666
I want one too!

05:39.250 --> 05:40.125
Fujino.

05:40.625 --> 05:43.583
Yeah. What is it, teacher?

05:43.666 --> 05:44.708
FACULTY'S OFFICE

05:44.791 --> 05:47.500
About the four-panel manga for next week,

05:48.083 --> 05:50.333
can I give one slot to Kyomoto?

05:50.916 --> 05:53.541
Kyomoto? Who's that?

05:53.625 --> 05:56.250
A truant student from the class next door.

05:56.333 --> 05:59.500
She can't come to school,
but wants to try drawing manga.

06:02.250 --> 06:04.416
I mean, I guess I don't mind.

06:04.500 --> 06:08.416
But drawing decent art
would be difficult for an amateur.

06:08.500 --> 06:13.375
I'm not sure a wimp who can't even
come to school can handle it.

06:14.416 --> 06:16.875
I'm handing out the newspaper.

06:16.958 --> 06:18.708
Don't forget to show it to your parents.

06:28.333 --> 06:30.208
AFTER SCHOOL BY KYOMOTO

06:45.291 --> 06:46.375
NO RUNNING IN THE HALL!

06:46.458 --> 06:47.291
SPORTS FESTIVAL

06:47.375 --> 06:48.416
SIR, YOU KNOW THE RULES.

06:48.500 --> 06:50.250
SHE CROSSED INTO SOMEONE ELSE'S LINE?

06:50.333 --> 06:54.125
MIKA THE SCHEMER BY FUJINO
AFTER SCHOOL BY KYOMOTO

07:00.208 --> 07:02.166
These are pro-level drawings.

07:02.250 --> 07:03.875
Hey, did you see it?

07:04.416 --> 07:06.625
Who's Kyomoto?

07:06.708 --> 07:08.416
She's the truant kid, right?

07:11.333 --> 07:12.833
But, you know,

07:12.916 --> 07:17.375
compared to Kyomoto's drawings,
yours look pretty average.

07:31.875 --> 07:35.291
Fujino, how come
you're so good at drawing?

07:36.916 --> 07:40.041
You have the best drawing skills
out of all my students.

07:41.916 --> 07:44.750
You could become an artist
with these skills.

07:47.541 --> 07:51.208
Compared to Kyomoto's drawings,
yours look pretty average.

08:03.958 --> 08:05.291
I see.

08:06.333 --> 08:12.041
Kyomoto must be practicing drawing
while I go to school.

08:20.250 --> 08:23.041
A fourth grader who's better
at drawing than me?

08:23.125 --> 08:25.208
Absolutely unacceptable!

08:29.791 --> 08:32.041
HOW TO GET BETTER AT DRAWING

08:32.625 --> 08:33.750
Welcome.

08:36.625 --> 08:37.916
Thank you.

08:42.291 --> 08:43.333
All right.

09:14.125 --> 09:15.875
SHORTCUTS TO IMPROVE
1. STUDY PERSPECTIVE

09:15.958 --> 09:17.125
2. LEARN ANATOMY
3. THINK 3D

09:17.208 --> 09:18.708
MOST IMPORTANTLY, JUST DRAW, STUPID!

09:35.250 --> 09:37.375
ANATOMY: COMPLETE GUIDE
BASICS OF FIRST-TIME DRAWING

10:11.791 --> 10:13.416
Let's go hang out somewhere.

10:13.500 --> 10:14.625
Wanna come to my place?

10:14.708 --> 10:16.208
Yeah! Are you sure?

10:18.416 --> 10:19.666
Fujino.

10:20.250 --> 10:21.541
What are you drawing?

10:25.125 --> 10:26.125
Hey.

10:26.708 --> 10:28.125
A human skeleton.

10:29.541 --> 10:32.125
Hey, we're sixth graders now, you know?

10:34.000 --> 10:37.708
We'll be in middle school next year.
Are you still gonna draw then?

10:38.375 --> 10:39.333
What?

10:40.000 --> 10:41.000
Yeah.

10:41.583 --> 10:43.333
I see.

10:44.791 --> 10:46.041
You know what?

10:46.125 --> 10:48.750
Yosshi and Mihorin haven't
been able to tell you this either,

10:50.000 --> 10:53.166
but aren't you getting
too old to keep drawing?

10:59.000 --> 11:02.916
You don't hang out with us anymore.

11:03.000 --> 11:05.791
Even when you do,
you're always drawing and you don't talk.

11:05.875 --> 11:06.875
Not to mention,

11:07.500 --> 11:09.791
if you keep drawing in middle school,

11:09.875 --> 11:12.791
people will think you're
a creepy otaku, you know?

11:15.000 --> 11:16.416
Kae, can we go now?

11:16.500 --> 11:17.333
Coming!

11:18.125 --> 11:19.250
Wait for me!

11:19.875 --> 11:23.166
Stop bothering her. She's drawing, right?

11:29.958 --> 11:32.333
Mom says hurry up
and take your bath already.

11:32.416 --> 11:35.541
Didn't I tell you to knock
before entering my room?

11:35.625 --> 11:36.458
Geez!

11:36.541 --> 11:37.833
Sheesh!

11:37.916 --> 11:39.416
Okay, okay.

11:39.500 --> 11:40.333
KNOCK FIRST

11:44.916 --> 11:48.500
How long are you gonna keep drawing manga?

11:50.250 --> 11:52.458
You should join my karate class.

11:52.541 --> 11:54.125
You can put it in your school report.

11:54.208 --> 11:55.625
Whatever.

11:56.166 --> 12:00.583
Mom and Dad don't say it,
but they're worried about you.

12:01.166 --> 12:05.250
You're always cooped up in your room
and your test scores are terrible.

12:07.083 --> 12:08.500
Get out.

12:28.125 --> 12:30.000
All right, quiet down.

12:30.083 --> 12:33.541
I'm handing out the newspaper.
Don't forget to show it to your parents.

12:35.083 --> 12:36.416
What will it be like?

12:38.958 --> 12:41.333
DAD! I MEAN, TEACHER.
I NEED TO USE THE BATHROOM.

12:41.416 --> 12:43.291
HEY! HE CALLED THE TEACHER HIS DAD!

12:43.375 --> 12:44.250
TEACHER

12:44.333 --> 12:45.250
HA HA HA HA

12:45.333 --> 12:47.333
HE ALSO NERVOUSLY TOUCHES HIS HAIR.
IS HE MY DAD?

12:47.416 --> 12:48.250
6TH GRADE NEWSPAPER

12:48.333 --> 12:50.125
TRUTH BY FUJINO
SUMMER FESTIVAL BY KYOMOTO

13:04.291 --> 13:05.625
I quit.

13:08.291 --> 13:11.166
What's wrong? Pass the newspaper, Fujino.

13:11.708 --> 13:12.541
Hey.

13:13.125 --> 13:15.458
Wanna go for ice cream after school?

13:16.000 --> 13:18.250
Really? Sure!

13:18.333 --> 13:20.958
We haven't hung out in ages.

13:22.166 --> 13:24.083
DRAWING
REVISION WORKSHOP

13:30.041 --> 13:32.916
KARATE

13:44.833 --> 13:46.500
KNOCK FIRST

13:52.916 --> 13:56.666
Mom! Could you throw these out too?

13:56.750 --> 13:59.625
GRADUATION!
BYE, EVERYONE!

14:06.000 --> 14:07.125
FACULTY'S OFFICE

14:07.208 --> 14:09.541
Hey, Fujino.
Congratulations on your graduation.

14:10.708 --> 14:12.583
I'm sorry, but I need a favor.

14:12.666 --> 14:15.541
Could you give this graduation diploma
to Kyomoto for me?

14:15.625 --> 14:17.166
I'll give you her address.

14:17.250 --> 14:20.708
What? Why me?

14:21.958 --> 14:26.541
Well, even if you quit drawing
in sixth grade,

14:26.625 --> 14:29.333
you guys still worked together
on the newspaper manga.

14:29.416 --> 14:32.583
I'm sure Kyomoto would rather get it
from you than from an old man like me.

14:32.666 --> 14:35.375
Well, I'd rather not, really.

14:35.458 --> 14:36.916
Oh, come on.

14:37.416 --> 14:39.541
Do your teacher one last favor.

14:40.541 --> 14:42.375
-Seriously?
-Here.

14:45.083 --> 14:46.958
KYOMOTO

14:59.083 --> 15:00.458
No one's home?

15:04.000 --> 15:05.208
It's open.

15:12.291 --> 15:13.666
Hello?

15:14.750 --> 15:18.000
I'm here to deliver
your graduation diploma.

15:23.625 --> 15:25.708
I'll leave it here, okay?

15:28.875 --> 15:30.083
Someone's home.

15:36.250 --> 15:37.458
Excuse me.

15:38.208 --> 15:41.541
I brought your graduation diploma.

16:29.958 --> 16:32.333
KYOMOTO'S HOUSE

16:35.083 --> 16:37.458
Don't come out! Don't come out!

16:37.541 --> 16:39.958
Come out! Come out!

16:41.125 --> 16:43.125
It's the world shut-in competition finals!

16:43.208 --> 16:46.041
Kyomoto is in first place
by a significant lead.

16:47.375 --> 16:50.500
KYOMOTO

16:58.416 --> 17:00.416
What am I even doing?

17:02.500 --> 17:03.333
Wait...

17:08.375 --> 17:09.333
No!

17:10.083 --> 17:11.041
Hey...

17:13.416 --> 17:16.083
I'm leaving your graduation diploma here!

17:16.916 --> 17:18.250
Goodbye!

17:33.125 --> 17:34.125
Fujino-sensei!

17:58.041 --> 17:59.166
Kyomoto?

18:13.291 --> 18:17.750
Every week, I got... I got the newspaper.

18:17.833 --> 18:22.208
I read your manga from the start,
since third grade.

18:23.791 --> 18:25.208
I... I...

18:25.291 --> 18:29.625
I'm a fan of yours, Fujino-sensei!

18:30.208 --> 18:31.625
Can I have your autograph?

18:34.833 --> 18:36.750
I don't have any paper!

18:38.000 --> 18:38.916
My back!

18:39.000 --> 18:41.291
Please sign the back of my jacket!

18:46.958 --> 18:47.916
Sure.

18:52.833 --> 18:57.416
My favorites are Love Square from the
second week of August in third grade,

18:57.500 --> 19:02.333
the Sasaki series you did
from January to March in fourth grade,

19:02.416 --> 19:07.125
and every single one
from fifth and sixth grades was brilliant.

19:07.208 --> 19:10.041
I couldn't always finish
my strips in time,

19:10.125 --> 19:12.958
but you did one every week
while attending school.

19:13.041 --> 19:15.833
I couldn't believe
you were a grade schooler like me.

19:16.291 --> 19:20.625
Your stories and drawings
kept getting better around fifth grade,

19:20.708 --> 19:22.375
I was sure of it.

19:23.666 --> 19:26.250
Fujino-sensei, you're a manga genius!

19:31.583 --> 19:33.500
So, why...

19:35.000 --> 19:39.583
Why did you stop drawing your strips
in the middle of sixth grade?

19:41.708 --> 19:43.083
Well, actually...

19:44.083 --> 19:47.083
I'm trying to come up with a story
for a manga competition.

19:47.166 --> 19:50.000
So basically,
I quit so that I could reach the next level.

19:51.750 --> 19:52.958
A manga competition?

19:55.500 --> 19:56.416
Amazing!

19:56.500 --> 19:59.708
I wanna see it! I totally wanna see it!
That's so amazing!

20:00.833 --> 20:02.458
I wanna see! I wanna see!

20:03.041 --> 20:06.083
Well, the idea's only in my head for now,

20:06.750 --> 20:08.875
but it's pretty much finished.

20:08.958 --> 20:11.916
Basically, all that's left
is to draw a draft and ink it.

20:13.875 --> 20:15.875
I wanna see! I wanna see!

20:18.750 --> 20:21.833
Then, I guess I could show you
when it's done.

20:30.291 --> 20:32.958
It's starting to rain. I should go.

20:34.375 --> 20:35.500
See you.

20:38.541 --> 20:39.625
See you.

21:58.833 --> 22:01.208
KNOCK FIRST

22:01.291 --> 22:04.166
METAL PARADE

22:18.500 --> 22:20.333
Wait for me.

22:23.333 --> 22:24.708
I'm home.

22:35.458 --> 22:36.541
Welcome back.

22:37.125 --> 22:40.125
You're still here?
Wait, you finished the background already?

22:40.708 --> 22:43.500
Yes. I don't go to school,
so it's a piece of cake.

22:44.291 --> 22:48.666
But it feels like we'll never
be able to finish all 45 pages.

22:48.750 --> 22:51.208
Yeah, and we've been drawing nonstop.

23:23.250 --> 23:25.625
METAL PARADE
BY KYO FUJINO

23:26.250 --> 23:28.208
You two middle schoolers really drew this?

23:28.291 --> 23:30.416
Amazing. I'm impressed.

23:31.041 --> 23:34.375
But it took us an entire year
to finish it.

23:35.041 --> 23:37.333
And she's done all the backgrounds.

23:37.916 --> 23:42.291
No, no. Being able to finish a manga
as a middle school student is a feat.

23:45.625 --> 23:48.041
The drawings and story
are both high quality.

23:48.125 --> 23:50.708
You could win an honorable mention
at the very least.

23:50.791 --> 23:53.000
METAL PARADE
BY KYO FUJINO

24:11.333 --> 24:13.958
WEEKLY JUMP

24:23.166 --> 24:25.041
RESULTS
13-YEAR-OLD DUO TAKES RUNNER-UP!

24:25.125 --> 24:27.500
1 MILLION YEN AWARD

24:27.583 --> 24:29.958
METAL PARADE
BY KYO FUJINO (13)

24:39.875 --> 24:40.708
Ta-da!

24:41.208 --> 24:43.125
I opened a bank account with my mom.

24:44.333 --> 24:45.500
Me too.

24:46.083 --> 24:48.083
And, guess what?

24:48.625 --> 24:49.458
Ta-da!

24:50.041 --> 24:51.666
I withdrew 100,000 yen.

25:01.708 --> 25:03.875
You could buy a house with that.

25:04.333 --> 25:05.916
Want to buy one?

25:07.458 --> 25:09.041
Let's go into town tomorrow.

25:09.625 --> 25:11.083
It's my treat.

25:11.666 --> 25:15.333
Don't you need to save that?

25:16.458 --> 25:20.000
Well, we're gonna draw more manga
and make loads of money anyway.

25:20.083 --> 25:23.458
So let's go eat tons of whipped cream
with this money.

25:27.000 --> 25:27.958
Yeah.

25:37.791 --> 25:39.708
CREPE FOREST

26:18.791 --> 26:21.166
Thank you for the treating me today.

26:21.833 --> 26:25.291
We spent like crazy,
but we only used 5,000 yen.

26:27.541 --> 26:30.333
I'm glad I came out of my room.

26:30.416 --> 26:31.250
What?

26:31.833 --> 26:36.291
To tell you the truth,
I was afraid to go out today.

26:37.250 --> 26:42.541
You see, I stopped going to school
because I was scared of people.

26:44.541 --> 26:49.041
But I had a really good time today.

26:50.458 --> 26:55.541
I started drawing because
I had nothing to do at home.

26:55.625 --> 26:58.666
But now I'm glad I did.

27:00.041 --> 27:03.833
Fujino, thank you
for getting me out of my room.

27:05.375 --> 27:07.416
You can thank me with 100,000 yen.

27:07.500 --> 27:08.333
What?

27:09.000 --> 27:09.958
Just kidding.

27:29.833 --> 27:31.458
THE SEA CITIES
BY KYO FUJINO

27:31.541 --> 27:32.708
MY HEART LIES WITH THE SEA

27:38.625 --> 27:41.583
THE CICADA HUMANS
BY KYO FUJINO

27:46.500 --> 27:48.041
THE MAN WHO ATE THE CRAB
BY KYO FUJINO

27:48.125 --> 27:49.500
BAGWORM
BY KYO FUJINO

28:16.625 --> 28:20.458
THE WORLD OF BACKGROUND ART

28:32.541 --> 28:34.291
We're getting serialized?

28:34.375 --> 28:37.583
The editor-in-chief wants you to try it
after you graduate high school.

28:37.666 --> 28:40.250
You've already had seven one-shots
published at age 17!

28:40.833 --> 28:42.791
Honestly, it's happening a little late.

28:56.875 --> 28:59.250
I'm sorry, I...

29:00.875 --> 29:03.375
I want to go to art school.

29:04.166 --> 29:05.083
So...

29:06.166 --> 29:07.125
So,

29:07.750 --> 29:10.000
I can't help with the series.

29:13.916 --> 29:16.000
Where's this coming from all of a sudden?

29:17.250 --> 29:19.916
Well, I guess it's fine.

29:20.000 --> 29:22.416
You only draw the backgrounds anyway.

29:22.500 --> 29:25.458
I can just get assistants to handle that.

29:28.500 --> 29:32.000
But there's no point
in going to art school.

29:32.083 --> 29:34.958
I heard there are no job prospects
even with an art degree.

29:35.875 --> 29:36.708
Yeah.

29:37.250 --> 29:38.750
I know...

29:38.833 --> 29:41.791
And you'll have to talk
to lots of strangers, you know?

29:42.708 --> 29:45.583
I'll work on that.

29:47.916 --> 29:51.583
If you just stick with me,
everything will work out.

29:58.125 --> 30:01.750
I want to try living on my own,

30:02.416 --> 30:04.791
without having to rely on you.

30:07.500 --> 30:09.583
It'll be so boring! I guarantee you!

30:10.166 --> 30:11.083
No, it won't!

30:11.666 --> 30:13.166
It totally will be!

30:13.250 --> 30:16.916
Not to mention, there's no way
you can handle college life on your own!

30:17.833 --> 30:19.750
I can! I will learn how!

30:19.833 --> 30:21.041
You'll fail!

30:21.125 --> 30:24.458
You're too shy to even talk
to the cashier at the convenience store!

30:24.541 --> 30:26.291
I'll practice.

30:26.375 --> 30:27.333
You can't pull it off!

30:27.416 --> 30:29.125
-But...
-What?

30:37.541 --> 30:38.583
I want to...

30:39.500 --> 30:41.291
get better at drawing.

30:57.208 --> 30:59.041
WEEKLY JUMP

30:59.125 --> 31:01.041
SHARK KICK SERIES RANKING

31:01.125 --> 31:03.291
SHARK KICK VOLUME 1
BY KYO FUJINO

31:07.833 --> 31:09.458
SHARK KICK VOLUME 2
BY KYO FUJINO

31:13.958 --> 31:15.583
SHARK KICK VOLUME 3
BY KYO FUJINO

31:53.750 --> 31:56.625
SHARK KICK SERIES RANKING

31:56.708 --> 32:00.083
KYO FUJINO

32:00.166 --> 32:04.458
SHARK KICK RANKED NO. 1
ANIME ADAPTATION CONFIRMED!

32:11.958 --> 32:15.708
Yes. She works diligently,

32:16.625 --> 32:18.541
but it's just not working out.

32:18.625 --> 32:20.041
Is there anyone else?

32:24.541 --> 32:28.375
Right, yes. I need more assistants.

32:32.416 --> 32:35.208
She's fast, but...

32:38.958 --> 32:41.458
She doesn't give enough thought
to the full picture.

32:42.000 --> 32:45.500
I know it's hard to find someone good.

32:45.583 --> 32:49.208
We have breaking news
from the Yamagata Broadcasting Station.

32:50.041 --> 32:53.875
Right. I'll just have to do
what I can for now.

32:58.000 --> 33:00.333
No, sorry again for the trouble.

33:00.833 --> 33:02.875
Let's discuss it again some other time.

33:04.750 --> 33:06.500
Okay. Bye.

33:19.000 --> 33:20.083
I repeat.

33:20.583 --> 33:24.875
Today at midday at an art university
in Yamagata City, Yamagata Prefecture,

33:24.958 --> 33:26.583
a man with no fixed address

33:26.666 --> 33:30.791
attacked students
using an axe-like weapon.

33:31.333 --> 33:36.500
The Yamagata police have arrested a man
believed to be the perpetrator.

33:37.250 --> 33:40.750
We are yet to receive
any information regarding the victims.

33:41.333 --> 33:47.291
The police are investigating the case
as a possible indiscriminate attack.

33:47.375 --> 33:48.875
CALLING
KYOMOTO

34:06.166 --> 34:08.041
MOM
INCOMING CALL

34:24.500 --> 34:27.625
If our manga ever gets serialized,

34:27.708 --> 34:29.625
I want the artwork
to be super high quality.

34:30.208 --> 34:32.750
But I draw really slow.

34:33.583 --> 34:36.083
I wish I could draw faster.

34:36.666 --> 34:38.125
That's easy.

34:38.666 --> 34:41.208
If your drawing skills improve,
so will your speed.

34:41.291 --> 34:43.541
I plan on improving mine.

34:44.125 --> 34:47.166
Then, I'll work on my drawing skills too.

34:47.791 --> 34:49.250
Like you, Fujino.

34:49.875 --> 34:54.083
Awesome. Keep your eyes on my back and you'll grow too.

35:07.208 --> 35:09.583
BREAKING NEWS
ART SCHOOL MASSACRE KILLER ARRESTED

35:09.666 --> 35:11.541
12 DEAD
3 GRAVELY INJURED

35:11.625 --> 35:14.000
STRUCK THE BODIES MULTIPLE TIMES

35:14.083 --> 35:16.958
"THE ART I POSTED ON THE INTERNET
WAS PLAGIARIZED"

35:17.041 --> 35:20.916
SHARK KICK HIATUS ANNOUNCEMENT
THANK YOU FOR ALL YOUR SUPPORT

36:08.166 --> 36:10.541
WEEKLY JUMP
SHARK KICK

37:16.083 --> 37:16.916
DON'T COME OUT!

37:17.000 --> 37:17.833
COME OUT! COME OUT!

37:17.916 --> 37:19.125
SHUT-IN COMPETITION FINALS!

37:19.208 --> 37:21.166
KYOMOTO IS IN FIRST PLACE
BY A SIGNIFICANT LEAD

37:21.250 --> 37:22.083
KYOMOTO

37:22.166 --> 37:25.041
DON'T COME OUT!

37:27.625 --> 37:30.250
COME OUT! COME OUT!

37:39.000 --> 37:40.250
It's my fault.

37:42.541 --> 37:44.208
It's because...

37:46.208 --> 37:47.833
I drew this manga that day.

37:57.291 --> 37:59.708
Kyomoto died...

38:00.833 --> 38:02.291
because of me.

38:04.125 --> 38:08.791
If I hadn't gotten her out of her room,
she wouldn't have died.

38:18.500 --> 38:19.333
Why?

38:21.791 --> 38:22.791
Why?

38:24.375 --> 38:26.583
Why did I draw this?

38:31.166 --> 38:33.958
Drawing is completely useless...

39:04.291 --> 39:06.000
"Don't come out"?

39:15.791 --> 39:17.125
Hello?

39:17.208 --> 39:20.000
I'm here to deliver
your graduation diploma.

39:21.166 --> 39:23.875
I'll leave it here, okay?

39:48.166 --> 39:49.916
Must be a ghost.

40:16.083 --> 40:17.958
LETTER OF ACCEPTANCE

40:37.875 --> 40:42.791
SECOND FLOOR OF THE ART DEPARTMENT
WESTERN ART COURSE BUILDING

40:49.250 --> 40:53.875
A STUDENT SITS ON A SOFA FOR A BREAK

40:53.958 --> 40:58.333
SHE HEARS A METALLIC KNOCKING SOUND
FROM THE STAIRCASE

41:01.916 --> 41:05.791
THERE ARE NO OTHER STUDENTS
NEAR THE SOFA

41:08.333 --> 41:12.208
AT 11:19 A.M., A MAN ENTERS FROM
THE OUTDOOR STAIRS AND SEES THE STUDENT

41:22.583 --> 41:26.458
HE IS HOLDING A POINTED TOOL
HE FOUND AT THE ART PRACTICE BUILDING

41:28.666 --> 41:29.666
Hey, you.

41:30.291 --> 41:31.291
I mean...

41:32.791 --> 41:34.291
You. I'm talking to you.

41:37.250 --> 41:38.500
At the exhibition,

41:38.583 --> 41:41.416
there was an artwork
that looked like mine, right?

41:44.125 --> 41:45.833
-My...
-Sorry?

41:48.833 --> 41:52.125
The artwork I posted online!
There was an exact copy, right?

41:52.208 --> 41:54.541
THE MAN SAID HE INTENDED TO KILL
ANY ART STUDENT HE SAW

42:13.000 --> 42:15.791
Don't you dare look down on me!

42:17.250 --> 42:19.041
That was my idea!

42:20.333 --> 42:22.416
You stole my art!

42:45.208 --> 42:48.250
I practice karate at the dojo
in the neighboring town.

42:48.333 --> 42:49.708
I was jogging

42:49.791 --> 42:52.333
when I saw this guy
going into campus with a weapon.

42:52.416 --> 42:54.083
I knew he was trouble,

42:54.166 --> 42:58.083
so I ran after him and when I gave him
a karate kick, I fell and broke my leg.

42:58.166 --> 42:59.541
Pretty lame, isn't it?

43:04.708 --> 43:06.708
Thank you very much.

43:07.541 --> 43:10.541
I'd like to thank you properly,

43:11.208 --> 43:14.916
so can I have your phone number?

43:15.500 --> 43:17.041
Yeah, sure thing.

43:20.583 --> 43:21.750
Fujino.

43:22.875 --> 43:24.250
Fujino-sensei.

43:24.916 --> 43:27.791
Are you Fujino-sensei by any chance?

43:28.416 --> 43:29.583
Sensei?

43:29.666 --> 43:31.208
When you were in grade school,

43:31.291 --> 43:34.541
did you draw four-panel manga strips
for the school newspaper?

43:35.125 --> 43:38.000
Yeah, I did, now that you mention it.

43:38.083 --> 43:39.541
It really is you!

43:39.625 --> 43:42.208
I was a fan of your four-panel manga.

43:43.541 --> 43:45.666
What a coincidence, right?

43:45.750 --> 43:47.000
Thanks.

43:47.083 --> 43:48.666
Sorry, but it's time to go.

43:56.458 --> 44:00.208
Why did you quit drawing manga?

44:06.125 --> 44:08.625
I recently started drawing again.

44:08.708 --> 44:11.250
If my manga gets serialized,
be my assistant, okay?

44:48.416 --> 44:49.625
I'm home.

45:08.875 --> 45:09.833
FIRST KISS BY FUJINO

45:09.916 --> 45:11.750
-KISS ME AGAIN WHEN WE'RE REINCARNATED.
-I WILL.

46:14.916 --> 46:17.833
-I'll kill you!
-Ahhh!

46:17.916 --> 46:19.291
-Take this!
-Agh!

46:20.250 --> 46:21.958
You're Fujino-sensei!

46:22.041 --> 46:23.583
You are not hurt?

46:24.250 --> 46:26.000
Then my work here is done.

46:27.625 --> 46:31.000
LOOK BACK BY KYOMOTO

47:21.291 --> 47:24.208
SHARK KICK BY KYO FUJINO

47:27.000 --> 47:29.625
READER QUESTIONNAIRE

47:45.458 --> 47:49.458
AYUMU FUJINO

47:56.333 --> 47:58.625
You know, for starters,

47:59.250 --> 48:01.750
I don't even like drawing manga.

48:02.291 --> 48:06.666
It's not fun, just plain tedious
and super unglamorous too.

48:07.375 --> 48:10.958
I can draw all day long
and still be nowhere near finished.

48:12.041 --> 48:13.958
I should stick to reading them.

48:14.750 --> 48:16.041
Drawing isn't for me.

48:22.708 --> 48:26.125
Then why do you draw, Fujino?

48:55.291 --> 48:57.583
METAL PARADE (WORKING TITLE)
BY AYUMU FUJINO

49:59.625 --> 50:02.541
SEPTEMBER
DEADLINE

50:28.041 --> 50:31.583
METAL PARADE

51:06.500 --> 51:12.500
IT'S SHARK TIME, BABY!
TO BE CONTINUED IN VOLUME 12!
